# `predev` / `predev:exposed` run `scripts/check-workspace-links.mjs` before the
# dev server starts, which is what catches a workspace member resolving to a
# registry copy instead of its source. pnpm 10 runs pre/post scripts by default,
# but the setting is opt-outable per user, and a dev who turned it off would
# lose the guard silently. Pin it here. (Until 2026-09-22 those hooks also ran
# `baml-generate`; the corpus and its committed client moved to
# `packages/harness-baml/` and nothing regenerates on the way in now.)
enable-pre-post-scripts=true
